From: Xianglong Kong <xkong@anaconda.com>
Date: 2026-07-01
Subject: [PATCH] Verify optional-dep availability with a real import

Upstream trl gates optional integrations with `if is_X_available():` blocks
across mergekit_utils.py, judges.py, callbacks.py, base_trainer.py,
scripts/vllm_serve.py, and every trainer that supports peft/wandb/liger/vllm/weave/...
The check itself is transformers.utils.import_utils._is_package_available,
which uses importlib.util.find_spec — that returns non-None in some conda
test envs even when the underlying package is not installed. The guarded
blocks then execute and crash with ModuleNotFoundError, breaking `trl --help`
and any downstream consumer that touches the trainer submodules (llamafactory's
`from trl import DPOTrainer` chain hits the same wall).

Iterate the `_X_available` module-level variables set above and re-verify each
one that reports True by attempting a real `__import__`. Iterating globals()
keeps this correct as upstream adds or removes availability entries — no
hardcoded parallel list to maintain.

---
--- a/trl/import_utils.py
+++ b/trl/import_utils.py
@@ -41,6 +41,21 @@
 _vllm_ascend_available = _is_package_available("vllm_ascend")
 _weave_available = _is_package_available("weave")
 
+# transformers._is_package_available uses importlib.util.find_spec, which returns
+# non-None in some conda envs even when the package is not actually importable
+# (namespace-package false positives, stale .dist-info, etc.).  Re-verify every
+# optional-integration boolean populated above by attempting a real __import__,
+# so `if is_X_available():` guards downstream never leak a ModuleNotFoundError.
+# Iterates the availability variables in globals() so this stays correct as
+# upstream adds/removes _X_available entries.
+for _var_name in [n for n in list(globals()) if n.startswith("_") and n.endswith("_available") and globals().get(n)]:
+    _pkg = _var_name[1:-len("_available")]
+    try:
+        __import__(_pkg)
+    except Exception:
+        globals()[_var_name] = False
+
+
 
 def is_deepspeed_available() -> bool:
     return _deepspeed_available
